  "3057": {
    "solution": [
      {
        "msg": "Zavedieme súradnice na $\\bold{V}$, s bázou $K = ((1, 0)^T, (0, 1)^T)$ pričom $(1, 0)^T = [(2, 1, 0, 1)]_K$ a $(0, 1)^T = [(1, 0, 1, 2)^T]_K$. Potom matica:\n$$\n[f]_K^K = \\left(\\begin{array}{cc} 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2 \\end{array}\\right)\n$$\n, čo sme dostali z podmienky. \n\nNech $B = ((2, 1)^T, (-1, 2)^T)$. Potom:\n$$\n[f]_B^B = \\left(\\begin{array}{cc} 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 \\end{array}\\right) \\\\\n[f^n]_B^B = \\left(\\begin{array}{cc} 2^n & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3^n \\end{array}\\right)\n$$ \nĎalej:\n$$\n[id]_B^K = \\frac{1}{5}\\left(\\begin{array}{cc} 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 \\end{array}\\right) \\\\\n[id]^K_B = \\left(\\begin{array}{cc} 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\end{array}\\right)\n$$\nTo znamená, že:\n$$\n[f^n]_K^K = \\left(\\begin{array}{cc} 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\end{array}\\right)\\left(\\begin{array}{cc} 2^n & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3^n \\end{array}\\right)\\frac{1}{5}\\left(\\begin{array}{cc} 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 \\end{array}\\right) = \n$$\nĎalej [(5, 1, 3, 7)^T]_K = (1, 3)^T. Takže:\n$$\n\\begin{align*}\n[f^n((5, 1, 3, 7)^T)]_K &= \\left(\\begin{array}{cc} 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\end{array}\\right)\\left(\\begin{array}{cc} 2^n & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3^n \\end{array}\\right)\\frac{1}{5}\\left(\\begin{array}{cc} 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 \\end{array}\\right)(1, 3)^T \\\\\n&=\\left(\\begin{array}{cc} 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\end{array}\\right)\\left(\\begin{array}{cc} 2^n & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3^n \\end{array}\\right)(1, 1)^T \\\\\n&=\\left(\\begin{array}{c} 2^n -3^n \\\\ 2^n + 2\\cdot 3^n \\end{array}\\right)\n\\end{align*}\n$$\nTo znamená, že $f^n((5, 1, 3, 7)^T) = (2^n - 3^n)(4, 1, 2, 5)^T + (2^n + 2 \\cdot 3^n)(1, 0, 1, 2)^T$."
      }
    ],
    "points": 2.0
  },
